r","text":"UTF8View"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can access a string’s view of UTF-8 code units by using its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"property. A string’s UTF-8 view encodes the string’s Unicode scalar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values as 8-bit integers."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let flowers = \"Flowers 💐\"","for v in flowers.utf8 {","    print(v)","}","\/\/ 70","\/\/ 108","\/\/ 111","\/\/ 119","\/\/ 101","\/\/ 114","\/\/ 115","\/\/ 32","\/\/ 240","\/\/ 159","\/\/ 146","\/\/ 144"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A string’s Unicode scalar values can be up to 21 bits in length. To"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent those scalar values using 8-bit integers, more than one UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"code unit is often required.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let flowermoji = \"💐\"","for v in flowermoji.unicodeScalars {","    print(v, v.value)","}","\/\/ 💐 128144","","for v in flowermoji.utf8 {","    print(v)","}","\/\/ 240","\/\/ 159","\/\/ 146","\/\/ 144"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the encoded representation of a Unicode scalar value, each UTF-8 code"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unit after the first is called a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"continuation byte"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":1,"text":"UTF8View Elements Match Encoded C Strings","type":"heading","anchor":"UTF8View-Elements-Match-Encoded-C-Strings"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift streamlines interoperation with C string APIs by letting you pass a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance to a function as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"text":" pointer. When you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"call a C function using a ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", Swift automatically creates a buffer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of UTF-8 code units and passes a pointer to that buffer. The code units"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of that buffer match the code units in the string’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" view.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example uses the C "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strncmp"},{"type":"text","text":" function to compare the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beginning of two Swift strings. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strncmp"},{"type":"text","text":" function takes two"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"const char*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pointers and an integer specifying the number of characters","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to compare. Because the strings are identical up to the 14th character,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comparing only those characters results in a return value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let s1 = \"They call me 'Bell'\"","let s2 = \"They call me 'Stacey'\"","","print(strncmp(s1, s2, 14))","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","print(String(s1.utf8.prefix(14))!)","\/\/ Prints \"They call me '\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Extending the compared character count to 15 includes the differing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters, so a nonzero result is returned.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["print(strncmp(s1, s2, 15))","\/\/ Prints \"-17\"","prin